# AKONY — Agent Rules
# Read by: Kilo Code, Cline, Roo, and any Cline-based AI extension

Read `src/documentation/AGENTS.md` for the full rule set and project context.

Key rules summary:
- Run `npm run dev` only — no separate backend. Supabase is the cloud backend.
- ALL work stays on branch `feature/k12-database-pivot`. Do NOT commit to `main`.
- RTL-first CSS (logical properties). Arabic-first UI.
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any`.
- NEVER break the Zustand store (`src/lib/stores/examStore.ts`).
- NEVER break the legacy PDF flow (Path B: Upload → Scope → Structure → Edit → Preview).
- When asked to "wrap up the session": check git status → ask for approval → commit → update `src/documentation/AKONY_MASTER.md` → overwrite `src/documentation/HANDOFF.md`.
- Read `src/documentation/HANDOFF.md` at session start to know where development was left.

## Minimize Prompts — Batch Everything
- NEVER run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push` as separate commands. Always chain: `git add -A; git commit -m "..."; git push origin [branch]`
- Chain file operations with semicolons in one command instead of multiple separate tool calls.
- Mark all read-only commands as safe to auto-run (git status, ls, cat, git log, tsc --noEmit).
- One commit per session. Accumulate changes, commit once at the end.
